      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Isn't that by design? the tutorial Tupper made says that the top most layer carries downwards. It's not that your 'arms on second' mask is being ignored, it's just that your top layer doesn't have arms on it at all.\nYou need to make a third layer, put it to the top, and make sure it has both arms AND legs. Then put only legs on the second one, only arms on the third. It'll start working. The top layer is telling VRchat to ignore the arms since it isn't in the first mask.\nhttps://ask.vrchat.com/t/av3-walkthrough-part-3-weights-blending-and-tracking/2139",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5f11ff92d47d3b367ec5e87b",
