      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "YandeRainy's comment below is correct. The PlayableLayer uses the mask on the top most layer to generate a \"total mask\". So you supply that on the top layer (which is always weighted 1).\nIf you have separate parts, use other layers, with individual masks that \"add up\" to this total mask. You can then weight these layers as needed. You can leave the top most layer empty except for the mask if you do not have animations that require the full mask.\nThe example Gesture layer shows this in action.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
